      "description": "The Honmaru Palace of Nagoya Castle, completed in 1615 as the residence of the Owari lords and destroyed in the 1945 air raids. The painstakingly reconstructed palace reopened in 2018 and is renowned for its gold-leaf wall paintings by the Kano school and intricate woodwork.",
